## Why This Is Asked
Tests privacy-aware distributed blind source separation, a realistic constraint in smart rooms. It probes understanding of distributed ICA, whitening, and robust updates under communication limits and node outages.

## Key Concepts
- Distributed ICA with local whitening and demixing
- Privacy-preserving statistics exchange (secure aggregation)
- Asynchronous synchronization and latency budgeting
- Missing data resilience and fault tolerance

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo: compute local whitening (illustrative only)
function localWhiten(X) {
  // X: channels x samples
  const cov = X.dot(X.transpose());
  // eigen-decomposition placeholder
  const { eigenVectors: V, eigenValues: D } = eigenDecompose(cov);
  const DinvSqrt = diagonalMatrix(D.map(v => 1 / Math.sqrt(v)));
  return DinvSqrt.multiply(V.transpose()).multiply(X);
}
```

